What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/<dev>/lock_state
Date:		October 2026
KernelVersion:	6.19
Contact:	Sam Winchenbach <sam.winchenbach@analog.com>
Description:
		(RO) Lock state of the ADSP-SC5xx part, one of:

		============  =============================================
		open          The part is not locked. OTP can be programmed.
		lock-pending  The lock is programmed, but it only takes
		              effect at the next reset. Until then no
		              further OTP programming is allowed. Read from
		              the OTP, so this survives rebinding or
		              reloading the driver.
		locked        The part is locked. OTP can no longer be
		              programmed.
		unlocked      The part is in the "unlocked" state (e.g. for
		              failure analysis). Customer OTP fields read as
		              zero and cannot be programmed.
		============  =============================================

What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/<dev>/lock
Date:		October 2026
KernelVersion:	6.19
Contact:	Sam Winchenbach <sam.winchenbach@analog.com>
Description:
		(WO) Writing the exact string "permanently-lock" permanently
		locks the part through the boot ROM. This cannot be undone.
		After the next reset the boot ROM only boots signed images and
		OTP access is restricted to secure bus requesters. Any other
		string is rejected with EINVAL.

		Root only.

		The write fails before anything is programmed, leaving the
		part unchanged, with:

		======  ===================================================
		EINVAL  The string written is not "permanently-lock".
		EPERM   The customer public key secure boot would use (the
		        first one not invalidated in boot_info) is blank, or
		        all are invalidated: a locked part only boots
		        streams authenticated with that key.
		EROFS   The part is already locked, "unlocked", or a lock is
		        pending, or the device is marked "read-only" in the
		        device tree.
		EBUSY   A SHARC+ core is neither held in reset nor idle
		        (silicon anomaly 20000084).
		======  ===================================================

		EIO means a failure of the OTP controller or the boot ROM:
		the OTP controller not ready or reporting an error, a failed
		OTP read, the ROM reporting a failure while programming the
		lock, or the lock not reading back as programmed. It can occur
		before or after the lock was programmed, so after EIO the part
		may already be locked. Read lock_state before proceeding:
		"lock-pending" means the lock is programmed and takes effect
		at the next reset, "open" that it is not.
